From dd051a0df43dbb94685d72d7f63b2b8a98ecca97 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daniel Campos Ramos <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 13:21:51 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 20/24] FFmpeg backend: decode depth maps with their pictures

A 2D plus depth video carries the depth map of its pictures in one of three
ways the FFmpeg backend did not follow: packed in the frame with the picture
(a Matroska track says the layout in its STEREO3D_LAYOUT tag), as the depth
auxiliary layer of an H.265 stream (AuxId 2, H.265 Table F.2), or as a
stream of its own (an ISO/IEC 23002-3 auxiliary video stream, MPEG-2
transport stream type 0x1E). A packed video showed both halves side by side
as one picture; of the other two only the pictures were shown.

With an FFmpeg that exports the depth (libavutil/multiview.h; Sparky Stereo
OS's FFmpeg +stereo3d5), and unless QT_FFMPEG_VIDEO_DEPTH=0:

- The layout of a packed video becomes the frame's depth StereoMode and
  StereoFlag::DepthFirst, the meaning of its samples (STEREO3D_DEPTH) the
  frame's stereoDepthMark().
- The H.265 decoder is asked for the pictures of the depth layer too
  (depth_output both); no hardware decoder outputs them, so such a stream
  is decoded in software, which getFormat() decides once the decoder says
  the stream has one (depth_available).
- An auxiliary depth stream is not offered as a video track: the demuxer
  reads it with the video, and its own decoder decodes it.

The stream decoder pairs each picture with the depth map of the same time
(raw streams without times in order), and packs the two side by side in one
frame of the picture's format: the depth map's samples as the luma of the
right half, at the picture's size and sample depth, with neutral chroma.
The frame says depthSideBySidePictureFirst, and its depth mark is what the
stream says: the depth representation information of H.264 (H.13.2.3) or
H.265 (G.14.3.4), with DMin and DMax counted in samples of the picture, or
the supplemental information of the ISO/IEC 23002-3 stream (nkfar and
nknear, or a parallax map's parallax_zero, parallax_scale and reference
width). A picture whose depth map does not come is shown alone.

The marks are those of Sparky Stereo OS (stereo-layer, docs/depth-marks.md);
the views are drawn by the consumer (VideoOutput).

